Z||000000||ferrari328||03-05-2001||05:20 PM||||Hi,<P>I saw in the galery these 2 interiors that i am interested in :<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/showpic.pl?Interior/cool_dash-4.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/showpic.pl?Interior/cool_dash-4.jpg</A> <BR>and <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/showpic.pl?Interior/kit1c.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/showpic.pl?Interior/kit1c.jpg</A> <P>I know that kitcaraccessories.com offers a ferrari replica interior but the $2000 US for it including the gauges is too expensive for me.<P>I live in toronto,ontario, canada and here are some pics of my ferrari 328 with V8 power :<BR> <A HREF="http://www.starsads.com/pics/masinamea.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.starsads.com/pics/masinamea.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.starsads.com/pics/ferrari2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.starsads.com/pics/ferrari2.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.starsads.com/pics/ferrari3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.starsads.com/pics/ferrari3.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.starsads.com/pics/ferrari4.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.starsads.com/pics/ferrari4.jpg</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-05-2001||07:59 PM||||I ordered a psudo ferrari dash from  <A HREF="http://usedfieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>http://usedfieroparts.com</A>  <P>about 3 weeks ago. It fits over the original pod gages and you have to move the accessory gauges into it and cover it. He uses themin his 355 Kits, and they come in F50 kits. Fiberglass, for $165.00 .........if I ever get it. Pics in the link under interior.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-06-2001||10:28 AM||||The 1st pic is of Eddy Snaaws dash (best looking dash I've ever seen).  He sold the molds to Scott Tilden from NV who intended (supposedly) to sell the dashes.  Unfortunately, Scott can't be reached and hasn't informed anyone of his current intent to sell.<P>The second pic is the Russian built Pyrana interior.  Unfortunately, they only made a couple of those and are now out of business.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||03-06-2001||12:21 PM||||MM, do you think this guy would go to a show like Carlisle?  I don't know anything about him but would love to talk with him to ask if he would make the dashes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||03-06-2001||05:08 PM||||Here's the story on Scott Tilden as I know it.<P>Eddy Snaaw wanted to sell the molds to someone in the States for the sole purpose of making and selling his dashes.  Scott Tilden said that he would do so.  I spoke to Scott after the sale regarding availability, pricing, etc.  Scott made it clear that he wanted to fix a few design "flaws" before he started production.  He mentioned $1500 for a bare dash.  For some reason, Scott seems to have disappeared.  He won't answer any emails or calls (I've lost his #.  Sorry.)  As far as I know, he's never made any completed dashes.  Hopefully, Eddy will sell another set of molds to someone who will use them to benefit the Fiero community.  <P>I can't afford a $1500 dash, but if the dash ever comes on the market, I'll find a way to be 1st in line.||||reg||1
